# The Taskboard mock API, one request per idea, with a body that works. The API panel sends these
# (so do VS Code's REST Client and JetBrains' HTTP Client). Paths are relative to the API, which
# listens on the port it prints (the workspace's API_PORT); the Vite dev server forwards /v1,
# /healthz, and /_hu to it, so the same paths also work against WEB_PORT.
#
# Sent top to bottom after npm run api:reset, each request gets what its > lines say. Logging in
# sets the tb_session cookie, which every later request sends, the way a browser does. The full
# contract, with every rule and status, is checked by content/contracts/taskboard/acceptance.http.

@password = correct horse battery staple

### Liveness, outside /v1
GET /healthz

> status 200
> json $ == {"status": "ok"}

### Not logged in: a 401 problem
GET /v1/me

> status 401
> header Content-Type ~ ^application/problem\+json
> header WWW-Authenticate ~ ^Bearer

### Log in as Ada: a token, and the same token in an HttpOnly cookie
# @name login
POST /v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ada@example.com", "password": "{{password}}"}

> status 200
> json $.user.name == "Ada Lovelace"
> json $.expires_at == "2026-10-02T09:00:00Z"
> header Set-Cookie ~ ^tb_session=[^;]+; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/$

### Who am I (the cookie answers)
GET /v1/me

> status 200
> json $ == {"id": 1, "role": "admin"}

### The same with the bearer token, as a mobile app or a script would send it
GET /v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

> status 200
> json $.email == "ada@example.com"

### My projects, with task counts
GET /v1/projects

> status 200
> json $[*].name == ["Website Relaunch", "Mobile App"]
> json $[0].task_counts == {"todo": 3, "doing": 3, "done": 2}

### One project, with its members
GET /v1/projects/1

> status 200
> json $.members[*].name == ["Ada Lovelace", "Grace Hopper"]

### Counts by status (the Stats tab)
GET /v1/projects/1/stats

> status 200
> json $ == {"todo": 3, "doing": 3, "done": 2}

### The board's request: every task, by due date
GET /v1/projects/1/tasks?sort=due&order=asc&limit=100&offset=0

> status 200
> json $.total == 8
> json $.items[0].title == "Set up analytics"

### Filters: to-do tasks only
GET /v1/projects/1/tasks?status=todo&sort=due

> status 200
> json $.items[*].id == [2, 5, 7]

### Search the title and the description (2 characters at least)
GET /v1/projects/1/tasks?q=login

> status 200
> json $.items[*].title == ["Fix login redirect"]

### Tasks with the bug label (the labels tier)
GET /v1/projects/1/tasks?label=bug

> status 200
> json $.items[*].id == [1]
> json $.items[0].labels[*].name == ["bug", "design"]

### A sort the API doesn't know: 400, naming the parameter
GET /v1/projects/1/tasks?sort=password

> status 400
> json $.errors.sort == $string

### Create a task: it starts in todo, at version 1
# @name created
POST /v1/projects/1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Write the launch email", "priority": 3, "due_on": "2026-10-12", "assignee_id": 2}

> status 201
> header ETag == "v1"
> json $ == {"title": "Write the launch email", "status": "todo", "priority": 3, "version": 1, "created_at": "2026-10-01T09:00:00Z"}

### A title of only spaces: 422, with the field in errors
POST /v1/projects/1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "   "}

> status 422
> json $.errors.title == "is required"

### Read it back, with its ETag
GET /v1/tasks/{{created.response.body.$.id}}

> status 200
> header ETag == "v1"

### Edit it, sending the version you read in If-Match
PATCH /v1/tasks/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "v1"

{"title": "Write the launch emails"}

> status 200
> header ETag == "v2"
> json $.version == 2

### Edit again with the old version: 412, with the task as it is now
PATCH /v1/tasks/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "v1"

{"priority": 1}

> status 412
> json $.current.title == "Write the launch emails"

### No If-Match at all: 428
PATCH /v1/tasks/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"priority": 1}

> status 428

### Move it to Doing: status changes only go through transition
POST /v1/tasks/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/transition
Content-Type: application/json

{"to": "doing"}

> status 200
> json $ == {"status": "doing", "version": 3}

### Done goes back only to doing, so done to todo is a 422
POST /v1/tasks/6/transition
Content-Type: application/json

{"to": "todo"}

> status 422
> json $.errors.to == $string

### The first 10 of task 1's 23 comments, oldest first
# @name page1
GET /v1/tasks/1/comments?limit=10

> status 200
> json $.items == $len:10
> json $.next_cursor == $string

### The next 10, after the cursor
GET /v1/tasks/1/comments?limit=10&cursor={{page1.response.body.$.next_cursor}}

> status 200
> json $.items[0].id == 11

### Comment on a task
POST /v1/tasks/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{"body": "Drafts are in the shared folder."}

> status 201
> json $.author == {"id": 1, "name": "Ada Lovelace"}

### This mock's switch for a failing request: a body with #fail answers 500
POST /v1/tasks/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{"body": "Please break #fail"}

> status 500

### Who watches task 1
GET /v1/tasks/1/watchers

> status 200
> json $[*].name == ["Ada Lovelace", "Grace Hopper"]

### Watch the new task (your own user id, from /v1/me)
PUT /v1/tasks/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/watchers/1

> status 204

### Project 1's labels, with how many tasks carry each
GET /v1/projects/1/labels

> status 200
> json $[*].name == ["backend", "bug", "design", "docs"]

### Put the bug label (id 1) on the new task
PUT /v1/tasks/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/labels/1

> status 204

### Find people (this route is slow on purpose: 440 ms for two letters)
GET /v1/users?q=gr

> status 200
> json $ == [{"id": 2, "name": "Grace Hopper", "email": "grace@example.com"}]

### Slow on purpose: X-HU-Delay answers after 1.5 seconds
GET /v1/projects
X-HU-Delay: 1500

> status 200

### Failing on purpose: X-HU-Fail answers with that status
GET /v1/projects
X-HU-Fail: 503

> status 503

### Delete the new task: owners only (Ada owns Website Relaunch)
DELETE /v1/tasks/{{created.response.body.$.id}}

> status 204

### Log out: the cookie is cleared and the session ends
POST /v1/auth/logout

> status 204
> header Set-Cookie ~ ^tb_session=;

### The session is gone
GET /v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

> status 401

### For checks only, outside the contract: the request log, the stored rows, and a reset to the seed
GET /_hu/log

> status 200

###
GET /_hu/state

> status 200
> json $.tasks == $len:18

###
POST /_hu/reset

> status 204
